WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:07.080
The review exercise’s main goal was to identify,&nbsp;
find, and fix the errors in this code. Whenever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:12.680
we suspect errors in code, we should inspect&nbsp;
the code for possible obvious errors and use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:18.720
any hints we get within the code editor&nbsp;
to find syntax errors. When in doubt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:25.760
run the code and see if errors come up. I will&nbsp;
run this code, and we see, in the traceback,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:37.120
a syntax error on line 7. Syntax errors will&nbsp;
usually be identified before runtime errors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.880
We should fix one error at a time, as fixing one&nbsp;
error could fix multiple errors. The syntax error&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:50.960
is that we have a space between the f and the&nbsp;
opening quotation mark in this f-string. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:59.880
may recall that a space is not allowed there. So,&nbsp;
I will remove that space. When you fix an error,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:07.520
you should run the code immediately to ensure the&nbsp;
fix works. I will rerun the code, and the syntax&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:22.240
error is gone, but there is a runtime error on&nbsp;
line 8. The error indicates that the equal sign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:31.360
is not allowed as a symbol to align text. The&nbsp;
symbol should be less than 15 to get this value&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:38.600
to take 15 spaces. Even if you don’t remember the&nbsp;
exact phrasing of an alignment symbol, one way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:45.560
try to fix an error is to react directly to what&nbsp;
you’re being told. The equal sign is not allowed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:54.920
so we should remove it, which is what I will do.&nbsp;
I will rerun the code, and now the code works as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.920 --> 00:02:01.400
anticipated. Again, look over code for possible&nbsp;
errors, and run code when in doubt about errors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:07.080
as Python will help you find both syntax&nbsp;
and runtime errors. For logical errors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:15.280
you may need to test code in multiple ways to see&nbsp;
where the logic has gone wrong within the code.

